title: The Heidelberg Congress
subtitle: The party congress meets in secret in Baden.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1919 and month = 10 and crisis = 0 and heidelberg_outcome = 0 and congress = 0
max-visits: 1
priority: 3
on-arrival: {!
Q.heid_already = (Q.ultraleft_gone || Q.ultraleft_strength < 3) ? 1 : 0;
Q.heid_fight = 0;
Q.heid_motion = 0;
if (Q.heid_already) {
    Q.heid_support = 90;
} else {
    RG.congressStart({id: 'heidelberg', name: 'The Heidelberg Congress', stake: 'The Zentrale\'s theses, and whether the Left Radicals stay in the party',
        sessions: 3, positions: ['luxemburgist', 'ultraleft'], backing: 'luxemburgist', kind: 'motion',
        mandates: ['members', 'zentrale', 'districts'][Q.heid_mandates] || 'members', delegates: 50, ownClose: true});
    // what the party has been through this year weighs on the delegates before anyone speaks
    var clamp = function (v, lo, hi) { return Math.max(lo, Math.min(hi, v)); };
    var h = Q.history_luxemburgist + Q.history_unionist + 0.5 * Q.history_offensive - 1.5 * Q.history_ultraleft;
    var m = clamp(h / 300, -0.06, 0.06) + clamp((Q.unity - 50) / 1000, -0.03, 0.03);
    if (Q.luxemburg_alive) { m += 0.08; }
    if (Q.natbol_line == 2) { m -= 0.03; }
    if (Q.heid_natbol == 1) { RG.congress.convert('hamburg', 0.2); RG.congress.convert('bremen', 0.25); }
    if (Q.heid_left == 1) { RG.congress.convert('berlin', 0.15); }
    if (m > 0) { RG.congress.sway(m); }
    if (m < 0) { RG.congress.swayTo('ultraleft', -m); }
    RG.congress.tally();
    Q.heid_support = Q.congress_votes_for;
}
Q.heid_for = Math.round(50 * Q.heid_support / 100);
Q.heid_against = 50 - Q.heid_for;
RG.news('Communists meet in secret congress: the boycotters face expulsion', 3);
!}

= The Heidelberg Congress

The second congress of the party opens near Heidelberg on 20 October, moving between inns and back rooms so that the police cannot find it. The theses are the only real business.

[? if heid_already = 0 : The Left Radicals have come to fight. Laufenberg and Wolffheim of Hamburg, Otto Rühle of Dresden and the Bremen delegates have a motion of their own: the unions are the bosses' police, parliament is a swamp, and a party with a Zentrale is a party of generals. Before the first session the Zentrale's people count the hall: about **[+ heid_for +]** of the fifty delegates look ready to vote for the theses. ?][? if heid_already = 1 : The Left Radicals are not in the hall. Their districts broke with the Zentrale months ago. The congress has only to say what that break means. ?] [? if luxemburg_alive = 1 and heid_already = 0 : Many who doubt the theses will not vote against Luxemburg herself. ?]

- @expel: Put the theses, the last one included.
- @soft: Put the theses without the expulsion clause.
- @withdraw: Withdraw the theses, and let each district choose its tactics.
- @confirm: Adopt the theses, and declare the break final.

@expel
view-if: heid_already = 0
subtitle: A clean party at a heavy price, and the harder vote to win.
on-arrival: {!
Q.heid_motion = 1;
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 3;
Q.lean_ultraleft -= 2;
RG.congress.bitter(6);
RG.congress.lose(0.04);
!}
go-to: mood

@soft
view-if: heid_already = 0
subtitle: Easier to carry. It settles nothing.
on-arrival: {!
Q.heid_motion = 2;
Q.lean_unionist += 2;
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 1;
RG.congress.bitter(2);
RG.congress.sway(0.06);
!}
go-to: mood

@withdraw
subtitle: No vote and no split. The party stays together on the Left Radicals' terms, and Lenin will be appalled.
view-if: ultraleft_gone = 0 and heid_already = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.heid_motion = 4;
Q.lean_ultraleft += 3;
Q.lean_luxemburgist -= 2;
Q.heidelberg_outcome = Q.heid_support < 55 ? 3 : 2;
Q.election_boycott = 1;
// no vote is taken: the congress disperses without a count
Q.congress = 0;
Q.congress_closing = 0;
Q.congress_heidelberg = 3;
Q.congress_name = 0;
Q.congress_stake = 0;
RG.ecci('lenin', -6);
!}
go-to: e19_heid_vote.result

@confirm
view-if: heid_already = 1
subtitle: The break has happened. The congress only names it.
on-arrival: heidelberg_outcome = 1; election_boycott = 0; lean_luxemburgist += 2
go-to: e19_heid_vote.result

@mood

= The First Session

[+ party_chair +] reads the theses. [? if heid_motion = 1 : The last of them is read slowly: whoever rejects these principles stands outside the party. Laufenberg is on his feet before the reading is over. ?][? if heid_motion = 2 : The last thesis, the one about expulsions, has been struck out. The Left Radicals are suspicious of the gift. ?]

At the end of the first evening the count stands at **[+ congress_votes_for +]%** for our motion[? if congress_ahead = 0 : , and the [+ congress_leader_name +] are ahead?].
